{
  "id": "public-app-bootstrap-callpath-index-ts-app-init-appwrapper-r",
  "title": "public/app bootstrap callpath: index.ts → app.init() → AppWrapper → routes",
  "kind": "callpath",
  "answers": [
    "How does the Grafana frontend boot up?",
    "Where does control flow from page load to route rendering in public/app?",
    "What is the entry point for public/app?"
  ],
  "body": "Boot sequence: `public/app/index.ts` awaits injected `bootData`, dynamically imports `public/app/initApp.ts`, which calls `app.init()` in `public/app/app.ts` (`GrafanaApp.init()`). That registers runtime services (`setBackendSrv`, `setDataSourceSrv` from `@grafana/runtime`), calls `configureStore()` (`public/app/store/configureStore.ts`), `initAlerting()`, `preloadPlugins()`, then renders `<AppWrapper>` via `createRoot(...).render()`. `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` wraps `<Provider store={store}>` + theme/context providers and renders routes from `getAppRoutes()` in `public/app/routes/routes.tsx`. Matched routes are gated/rendered by `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx:GrafanaRouteWrapper` (auth/role checks) before the page component mounts. All backend HTTP access goes through `public/app/core/services/backend_srv.ts` (`BackendSrv`), reached anywhere via `getBackendSrv()` from `@grafana/runtime`.",
  "tags": [
    "public/app",
    "bootstrap",
    "routing",
    "frontend"
  ],
